-- title:
--   Deformations of an affine chart modulo a square-zero ideal are automorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $T'$ be a commutative ring and $I \subseteq T'$ an ideal with $I \cdot I = \bot$. Let $Y$ be a scheme with a morphism $q_Y \colon Y \to \operatorname{Spec} T'$, let $U$ be an open of $Y$ which is affine (`hU`), and give $\Gamma(Y,U)$ the $T'$-algebra structure `algebraOfHom qY U`, i.e. the one coming from the ring map $(\Gamma\!-\!\mathrm{Spec}$ iso$)^{-1}$ followed by $q_Y.\mathrm{appLE}\ \top\ U$. Let $v \colon \operatorname{Spec}\Gamma(Y,U) \to Y$ be a morphism such that $v$ followed by $q_Y$ equals `hU.fromSpec` followed by $q_Y$, and such that $v$ and `hU.fromSpec` agree after precomposition with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $\Gamma(Y,U) \to \Gamma(Y,U)/J$, where $J = I\,\Gamma(Y,U)$ is the ideal generated by the image of $I$. Then there is an isomorphism $\tau$ of the scheme $U$ with itself such that: `hU.isoSpec.inv` followed by $\tau$ and by the inclusion $U \hookrightarrow Y$ equals $v$; $\tau$ followed by the inclusion and $q_Y$ equals the inclusion followed by $q_Y$; $\tau$ pulls back every open $O$ of $U$ to itself; and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map followed by `hU.isoSpec.inv` and $\tau$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map followed by `hU.isoSpec.inv`.
--
--   This is the standard rigidity statement in infinitesimal deformation theory: two morphisms from the spectrum of the sections of an affine open into the ambient scheme which agree modulo a square-zero ideal differ by an automorphism of that open which is the identity on the underlying topological space and congruent to the identity modulo the ideal. It is used in the comparison of local coordinates on overlapping charts for small extensions, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_overlap_iso_isTangentCoordsOfPairAtVia_of_pointDerivations`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_overlap_iso_isTangentCoordsOfPairAtVia_of_pointDerivations).
